  "title": "GenerateReqInput normalization is not an exactly-one input-form contract",
  "mechanism": "GenerateReqInput normalization at the pinned revision rejects an all-empty input and a simultaneous text/input_ids/input_embeds triple. The actual predicates still allow pairs. In the text branch it clears input_embeds but does not clear input_ids, so the excerpts do not support an exactly-one-form invariant. Bootstrap normalization expands a scalar bootstrap_room across a batch with per-item offsets in the shown branch. __getitem__ constructs and caches a per-request object by indexing selected normalized fields; this is not a fresh general validation pass and it does not prove every field has been independently shape-checked.",
  "corrections": [
    "Replace the candidate exactly-one claim with the two actual rejection predicates.",
    "Distinguish bootstrap normalization from per-item extraction.",
    "No end-to-end multimodal, streaming or transport conformance was tested."
  ],
  "source_scope": "Manually read the listed exact Git ranges for the final corrected mechanism. All other model claims remain research notes; no runtime experiment.",
